title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1926 and inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/Inter_Party.png
max-visits: 12
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Poland.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The <span style="color: #DD0000;">PPS</span> cannot govern by itself yet. Because we do not have an electoral majority, we need the support of other parties. We have only been able to enter governments consisting of the PSL-W, PSL-P, and other Democratic parties. We can reach out and build additional connections with these parties, or perhaps we can stand alone.

- @peasant: Strengthen our bonds with the <span style="color: #80FF00;">PSL-"Liberation"</span> and left-agrarian <span style="color: #179900;">PSL-"Left"</span>.
- @piast: Strengthen our bonds with the conservative <span style="color: #3A6538;">PSL-"Piast"</span>.
- @bmn: Strengthen our bonds with centrist <span style="color: #E3AF34;">Minority Parties</span>.
- @npr: Strengthen our bonds with the conservative left <span style="color: #841839;">NPR</span>.
- @pps_alone: The <span style="color: #DD0000;">PPS</span> can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard

@peasant
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; psl_l_relation += 8; psl_w_relation += 8

We are ideologically close with them so it is easy to build relations with the PSL-L.

@piast
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: piast_op if psl_p_in_government = 1 and pps_in_government = 0; piast_coalition if pps_in_government = 1 and psl_p_in_government = 1

@piast_op
on-arrival: psl_p_relation += 4*(1 - dissent); psl_p_relation += 2*(1 - dissent) if pps_toleration; psl_p_relation -= 3 if lanckorona_pact = 1

[? if pps_toleration != 1 : We are currently in opposition to the current government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will. ?][? if pps_toleration : We are currently tolerating the government, so we are able to build relations with them. ?][? if lanckorona_pact : However the rightward turn of the <span style="color: #3A6538;">PSL-P</span> has made building relations difficult, but not impossible ?]

@piast_coalition
on-arrival: psl_p_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); psl_p_relation -= 4 if lanckorona_pact = 1

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally. [? if lanckorona_pact : However the rightward turn of the <span style="color: #3A6538;">PSL-P</span> has made building relations difficult, but not impossible ?]

@bmn
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; bmn_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)
go-to: bmn_coalition if bmn_in_government and pps_in_government = 1

We are able through build a relationship with the <span style="color: #E3AF34;">BMN</span>.

@bmn_coalition
on-arrival: bmn_relation += 5

We are currently coalition partners with them, and historically, they haven't been able to enter the government without our help so improving relations comes naturally.

@npr
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; npr_relation += 8

We are able to improve our relations with the NPR as we are ideologically similar in economic issues with the difference being that they are a conservative party.

@pps_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
